What:           /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/capture_abi
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        PlutoSDR experimental receiver contributors
Description:
                PIL1-1.0-upper-only identifies experimental post-decimation
                single-RX CI16 pilot capture. It is not the production dual-RX
                equal-rate metadata ABI. sampling_frequency is read-only
                2500000; the PHY remains at its separate full source rate.

What:           /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/capture_visit_id
What:           /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/capture_sample_limit
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        PlutoSDR experimental receiver contributors
Description:
                Unsigned decimal u32 configuration, writable only with buffers
                disabled. A nonzero visit ID must be explicitly set before
                enabling capture. Limit 0 means continuous. A positive limit
                must be a multiple of the requested IIO buffer length and
                stops after exactly that many supported complex output samples.
                Both I and Q must be enabled; driver refuses partial scan masks.
                Full source clock rate must match the FPGA rate at enable.

What:           /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/capture_fault
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        PlutoSDR experimental receiver contributors
Description:
                Live capture fault bitmask, eight hexadecimal digits. Faults
                stop FPGA admission, not the already offered DMA prefix. This
                initial driver polls status; it does not enable the fault IRQ.
                Readers must check snapshots/faults and use bounded IIO waits.

What:           /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/capture_snapshot
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        PlutoSDR experimental receiver contributors
Description:
                One atomic hardware snapshot per sysfs read, serialized with
                capture control. ASCII whitespace-separated fields:
                PIL1 00010000 source_hz 2500000 generation recovery_failed
                actual_source_hz dma_error word0 ... word25
                Header numeric fields after version are decimal (dma_error
                is a signed kernel errno); each word is eight hexadecimal digits.
                Hardware words are latched together; actual clock/DMA error
                are contemporaneous software observations, not latched RF state.
                Word pairs are low/high unsigned 64-bit values:
                  0..1   first admitted newest canonical index
                  2..3   last admitted newest canonical index
                  4..5   admitted count
                  6..7   AXIS-delivered count
                  8..9   unsupported count
                  10..11 first fault diagnostic coordinate
                  12..13 DDC accepted count
                  14..15 DDC emitted count
                  16     DDC saturation count
                  17     DDC sticky faults [7:0], ingress high water [15:8]
                  18     capture faults
                  19     status: active/queued/fault/prefix/used bits 0..4
                  20     visit ID
                  21     output FIFO high water
                  22     output FIFO queued count
                  23..25 reserved zero
                Output sample j has original-source signal-center coordinate
                (first_index + 6*j - 269) * (source_hz / 15000000).
                No per-sample metadata is interleaved into the CI16 buffer.
                AXIS delivery does NOT prove DDR, host, or disk completion.
                Cancellation stops admission and drains before DMA abort. A
                bounded drain failure sets recovery_failed and refuses re-arm;
                it must be surfaced, never concealed by clearing buffered IQ.
                Hardware/DMA fault recovery remains a qualification gate.
